   {
    "id": "blockquote_00002",
    "type": "blockquote",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     13
    ],
    "text": "fstatat, lstat, stat — get file status",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00003",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     15
    ],
    "text": "[A2][/A2]SYNOPSIS",
    "placeholders": {
     "A2": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_190_02\" id=\"tag_17_190_02\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00004",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     17,
     1
    ],
    "text": "[CODE3]",
    "placeholders": {
     "CODE3": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<code><tt><sup>[<a href=\"javascript:open_code('OH')\">OH</a>]</sup> <img src=\"../images/opt-start.gif\" border=\"0\">#include\n&lt;fcntl.h&gt;<img src=\"../images/opt-end.gif\" border=\"0\"><br>\n#include &lt;<a href=\"../basedefs/sys_stat.h.html\">sys/stat.h</a>&gt;<br>\n<br>\nint fstatat(int fd, const char *restrict</tt> <i>path</i><tt>,<br>\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; struct stat *restrict</tt> <i>buf</i><tt>, int</tt> <i>flag</i><tt>);<br>\nint lstat(const char *restrict</tt> <i>path</i><tt>, struct stat *restrict</tt> <i>buf</i><tt>);<br>\nint stat(const char *restrict</tt> <i>path</i><tt>, struct stat *restrict</tt> <i>buf</i><tt>);<br></tt></code>"
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00005",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     19
    ],
    "text": "[A4][/A4]DESCRIPTION",
    "placeholders": {
     "A4": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_190_03\" id=\"tag_17_190_03\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00006",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     1
    ],
    "text": "The [I5]stat[/I5]() function shall obtain information about the named file and write it to the area pointed to by the [I6]buf[/I6]\nargument. The [I7]path[/I7] argument points to a pathname naming a file. Read, write, or execute permission of the named file is not\nrequired. An implementation that provides additional or alternate file access control mechanisms may, under implementation-defined\nconditions, cause [I8]stat[/I8]() to fail. In particular, the system may deny the existence of the file specified by [I9]path[/I9].",
    "placeholders": {
     "I5": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I6": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I7": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I8": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I9": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00007",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     3
    ],
    "text": "If the named file is a symbolic link, the [I10]stat[/I10]() function shall continue pathname resolution using the contents of the\nsymbolic link, and shall return information pertaining to the resulting file if the file exists.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I10": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00008",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     5
    ],
    "text": "The [I11]buf[/I11] argument is a pointer to a [B12]stat[/B12] structure, as defined in the [A13][I14]&lt;sys/stat.h&gt;[/I14][/A13] header, into which information is placed concerning the file.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I11": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "B12": {
      "open": "<b>",
      "close": "</b>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A13": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../basedefs/sys_stat.h.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I14": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00009",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     7
    ],
    "text": "The [I15]stat[/I15]() function shall update any time-related fields (as described in XBD [A16][I17]4.12 File Times Update[/I17][/A16]), before writing into the [B18]stat[/B18] structure.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I15": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A16": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../basedefs/V1_chap04.html#tag_04_12\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I17": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "B18": {
      "open": "<b>",
      "close": "</b>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00010",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     9
    ],
    "text": "[S19][[A20]SHM[/A20]][/S19] [IMG21]\nIf the named file is a shared memory object, the implementation shall update in the [B22]stat[/B22] structure pointed to by the\n[I23]buf[/I23] argument the [I24]st_uid[/I24], [I25]st_gid[/I25], [I26]st_size[/I26], and [I27]st_mode[/I27] fields, and only the S_IRUSR, S_IWUSR,\nS_IRGRP, S_IWGRP, S_IROTH, and S_IWOTH file permission bits need be valid. The implementation may update other fields and flags.\n[IMG28]",
    "placeholders": {
     "S19": {
      "open": "<sup>",
      "close": "</sup>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A20": {
      "open": "<a href=\"javascript:open_code(&#x27;SHM&#x27;)\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "IMG21": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<img src=\"../images/opt-start.gif\" alt=\"[Option Start]\" border=\"0\">"
     },
     "B22": {
      "open": "<b>",
      "close": "</b>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I23": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I24": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I25": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I26": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I27": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "IMG28": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<img src=\"../images/opt-end.gif\" alt=\"[Option End]\" border=\"0\">"
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00011",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     11
    ],
    "text": "[S29][[A30]TYM[/A30]][/S29] [IMG31]\nIf the named file is a typed memory object, the implementation shall update in the [B32]stat[/B32] structure pointed to by the\n[I33]buf[/I33] argument the [I34]st_uid[/I34], [I35]st_gid[/I35], [I36]st_size[/I36], and [I37]st_mode[/I37] fields, and only the S_IRUSR, S_IWUSR,\nS_IRGRP, S_IWGRP, S_IROTH, and S_IWOTH file permission bits need be valid. The implementation may update other fields and flags.\n[IMG38]",
    "placeholders": {
     "S29": {
      "open": "<sup>",
      "close": "</sup>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A30": {
      "open": "<a href=\"javascript:open_code(&#x27;TYM&#x27;)\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "IMG31": {
      "open": "",
