   {
    "id": "h5_00056",
    "type": "h5",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     37,
     1
    ],
    "text": "[A99][/A99]Obtaining File Status Information",
    "placeholders": {
     "A99": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_190_06_01\" id=\"tag_17_190_06_01\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00057",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     37,
     3
    ],
    "text": "The following example shows how to obtain file status information for a file named [B100]/home/cnd/mod1[/B100]. The structure variable\n[I101]buffer[/I101] is defined for the [B102]stat[/B102] structure.",
    "placeholders": {
     "B100": {
      "open": "<b>",
      "close": "</b>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I101": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "B102": {
      "open": "<b>",
      "close": "</b>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h5_00058",
    "type": "h5",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     37,
     7
    ],
    "text": "[A103][/A103]Getting Directory Information",
    "placeholders": {
     "A103": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_190_06_02\" id=\"tag_17_190_06_02\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00059",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     37,
     9
    ],
    "text": "The following example fragment gets status information for each entry in a directory. The call to the [I104]stat[/I104]() function\nstores file information in the [B105]stat[/B105] structure pointed to by [I106]statbuf[/I106]. The lines that follow the [I107]stat[/I107]() call\nformat the fields in the [B108]stat[/B108] structure for presentation to the user of the program.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I104": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "B105": {
      "open": "<b>",
      "close": "</b>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I106": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I107": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "B108": {
      "open": "<b>",
      "close": "</b>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h5_00060",
    "type": "h5",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     37,
     13
    ],
    "text": "[A109][/A109]Obtaining Symbolic Link Status Information",
    "placeholders": {
     "A109": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_190_06_03\" id=\"tag_17_190_06_03\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00061",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     37,
     15
    ],
    "text": "The following example shows how to obtain status information for a symbolic link named [B110]/modules/pass1[/B110]. The structure\nvariable [I111]buffer[/I111] is defined for the [B112]stat[/B112] structure. If the [I113]path[/I113] argument specified the pathname for the file\npointed to by the symbolic link ([B114]/home/cnd/mod1[/B114]), the results of calling the function would be the same as those returned by\na call to the [I115]stat[/I115]() function.",
    "placeholders": {
     "B110": {
      "open": "<b>",
      "close": "</b>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I111": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "B112": {
      "open": "<b>",
      "close": "</b>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I113": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "B114": {
      "open": "<b>",
      "close": "</b>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I115": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
