    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00065",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     45,
     1
    ],
    "text": "The intent of the paragraph describing &quot;additional or alternate file access control mechanisms&quot; is to allow a secure\nimplementation where a process with a label that does not dominate the file's label cannot perform a [I118]stat[/I118]() function. This\nis not related to read permission; a process with a label that dominates the file's label does not need read permission. An\nimplementation that supports write-up operations could fail [A119][I120]fstat[/I120]()[/A119] function calls\neven though it has a valid file descriptor open for writing.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I118": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A119": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/fstat.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I120": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00066",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     45,
     3
    ],
    "text": "The purpose of the [I121]fstatat[/I121]() function is to obtain the status of files in directories other than the current working\ndirectory without exposure to race conditions. Any part of the path of a file could be changed in parallel to a call to\n[I122]stat[/I122](), resulting in unspecified behavior. By opening a file descriptor for the target directory and using the\n[I123]fstatat[/I123]() function it can be guaranteed that the file for which status is returned is located relative to the desired\ndirectory.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I121": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I122": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I123": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
