     61,
     1
    ],
    "text": "Large File Summit extensions are added.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00076",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     63
    ],
    "text": "[A150][/A150]Issue 6",
    "placeholders": {
     "A150": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_190_13\" id=\"tag_17_190_13\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00077",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     65,
     1
    ],
    "text": "In the SYNOPSIS, the optional include of the [A151][I152]&lt;sys/types.h&gt;[/I152][/A151] header is\nremoved.",
    "placeholders": {
     "A151": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../basedefs/sys_types.h.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I152": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00078",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     65,
     3
    ],
    "text": "The following new requirements on POSIX implementations derive from alignment with the Single UNIX Specification:",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00079",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     65,
     5,
     1,
     1
    ],
    "text": "The requirement to include [A153][I154]&lt;sys/types.h&gt;[/I154][/A153] has been removed. Although\n[A155][I156]&lt;sys/types.h&gt;[/I156][/A155] was required for conforming implementations of previous POSIX\nspecifications, it was not required for UNIX applications.",
    "placeholders": {
     "A153": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../basedefs/sys_types.h.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I154": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A155": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../basedefs/sys_types.h.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I156": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00080",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     65,
     5,
     3,
     1
    ],
    "text": "The [EIO] mandatory error condition is added.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00081",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     65,
     5,
     5,
     1
    ],
    "text": "The [ELOOP] mandatory error condition is added.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00082",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     65,
     5,
     7,
     1
    ],
    "text": "The [EOVERFLOW] mandatory error condition is added. This change is to support large files.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00083",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     65,
     5,
     9,
     1
    ],
    "text": "The [ENAMETOOLONG] and the second [EOVERFLOW] optional error conditions are added.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00084",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     65,
     7
    ],
    "text": "The following changes were made to align with the IEEE&nbsp;P1003.1a draft standard:",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00085",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     65,
     9,
     1,
     1
    ],
    "text": "Details are added regarding the treatment of symbolic links.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00086",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     65,
     9,
     3,
     1
    ],
    "text": "The [ELOOP] optional error condition is added.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00087",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     65,
     11
    ],
    "text": "The normative text is updated to avoid use of the term &quot;must&quot; for application requirements.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00088",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     65,
     13
    ],
    "text": "The [B157]restrict[/B157] keyword is added to the [I158]stat[/I158]() prototype for alignment with the ISO/IEC&nbsp;9899:1999 standard.",
    "placeholders": {
     "B157": {
      "open": "<b>",
      "close": "</b>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I158": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00089",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     67
    ],
    "text": "[A159][/A159]Issue 7",
    "placeholders": {
     "A159": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_190_14\" id=\"tag_17_190_14\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00090",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     69,
     1
    ],
    "text": "Austin Group Interpretation 1003.1-2001 #143 is applied.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00091",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     69,
     3
    ],
    "text": "XSH-SD5-ERN-161 is applied, updating the DESCRIPTION to clarify to which file types [I160]st_nlink[/I160] applies.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I160": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00092",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     69,
     5
    ],
    "text": "The [I161]fstatat[/I161]() function is added from The Open Group Technical Standard, 2006, Extended API Set Part 2.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I161": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00093",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     69,
     7
    ],
    "text": "Changes are made related to support for finegrained timestamps.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00094",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     69,
     9
    ],
    "text": "The [I162]lstat[/I162]() function is now required to return meaningful data for symbolic links in all [B163]stat[/B163] structure fields,\nexcept for the permission bits of [I164]st_mode[/I164].",
    "placeholders": {
     "I162": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "B163": {
      "open": "<b>",
      "close": "</b>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I164": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00095",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     69,
     11
    ],
    "text": "Changes are made to allow a directory to be opened for searching.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00096",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     69,
     13
    ],
    "text": "The [ENOTDIR] error condition is clarified to cover the condition where the last component of a pathname exists but is not a\ndirectory or a symbolic link to a directory.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00097",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     69,
     15
    ],
    "text": "POSIX.1-2008, Technical Corrigendum 1, XSH/TC1-2008/0198 [461], XSH/TC1-2008/0199 [324], XSH/TC1-2008/0200 [278],\nXSH/TC1-2008/0201 [278], and XSH/TC1-2008/0202 [291] are applied.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00098",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     69,
     17
    ],
    "text": "POSIX.1-2008, Technical Corrigendum 2, XSH/TC2-2008/0136 [591], XSH/TC2-2008/0137 [817], XSH/TC2-2008/0138 [817], and\nXSH/TC2-2008/0139 [889] are applied.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00099",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     71
    ],
    "text": "[A165][/A165]Issue 8",
    "placeholders": {
     "A165": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_190_15\" id=\"tag_17_190_15\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00100",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     73,
     1
    ],
    "text": "Austin Group Defect 1380 is applied, changing text using the term &quot;link&quot; in line with its updated definition.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00101",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     73,
     3
    ],
    "text": "Austin Group Defect 1409 is applied, changing the EXAMPLES section.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00102",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     79
    ],
    "text": "&nbsp;",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   }
  ]
 }
}